<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Moldavian Democratic Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1917 CE – 1918 CE · capital Chișinău</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Short-lived republic of Bessarabia proclaimed after the Russian Revolution, which voted for union with Romania in 1918.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the fall of the Russian monarchy in 1917, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bessarabia">Bessarabia's</a> Romanian-speaking majority organised politically. A regional council, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sfatul-tarii">Sfatul Țării</a>, met in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chisinau">Chișinău</a> and on 2 December 1917 proclaimed the Moldavian Democratic Republic as an autonomous member of a planned Russian federation, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ion-inculet">Ion Inculeț</a> as president.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The council, elected by soldiers' congresses, peasants and national groups, struggled to govern amid deserting soldiers, peasant land seizures and Bolshevik agitation. In January 1918 Romanian troops entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bessarabia">Bessarabia</a>, invited by part of the leadership, and drove out Bolshevik units. The republic proclaimed full independence on 24 January 1918, and land reform was a central issue.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>On 27 March 1918 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sfatul-tarii">Sfatul Țării</a> voted for union with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-romania">Kingdom of Romania</a>, under Romanian military presence. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Soviet Russia</a> never recognised the union, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> annexed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bessarabia">Bessarabia</a> in 1940; much of it is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moldova">Moldova</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/moldavian-democratic-republic.jpg" alt="Moldavian Democratic Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Лобачев Владимир · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:National_flag_of_the_Moldavian_Democratic_Republic.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1917 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Chișinău</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ion Inculeț, Pantelimon Erhan, Daniel Ciugureanu</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Eastern Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Romanian, Russian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/moldova">Moldova</a>, <a href="/countries/ukraine">Ukraine</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Moldavian Republic (1917), Bessarabian Republic</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=moldavian-democratic-republic" aria-label="Moldavian Democratic Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5356 527 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Moldavian Democratic Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5676 783L6487 457M5676 783L5624 863"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6487 457h0M5624 863h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5676 783h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5676 783h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Chișinău. <a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=moldavian-democratic-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
